  "term": "Gulf War syndrome",
  "definition": "Gulf War syndrome refers to a pattern of unexplained symptoms reported by veterans of the 1991 Persian Gulf War. These symptoms can include fatigue, pain, headaches, memory loss, breathing and digestive problems, skin rash, and unusual sensitivity to common chemicals.",
